                <pb facs="0399" n="381" xml:id="pg381"/>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pertinent Assumptions</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">Indochina</hi></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item><hi rendition="#italic">MDAP and
                            Common-use Programs</hi> (Col. 2) expenditures assume (a) elimination of
                        organized resistance by June 1955; (b) a period of pacification extending
                        for approximately another year; (c) a continuance of U.S. assistance for the
                        duration of the major military operations at approximately the same rate as
                        in FY 1954.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item><hi rendition="#italic">Financial Support through France</hi> (Col. 3)
                        expenditures for FY 1950–53 reflect staff
                        estimates of amounts of aid to France which is attributable to
                        Indochina.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item><hi rendition="#italic">Economic Assistance</hi> (Col. 4) includes no
                        specific estimates for rehabilitation on the assumption that such costs
                        could be offset against reduced military expenditures.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item><hi rendition="#italic">Informational Activities</hi> (Col. 5) are assumed
                        to continue in FY 1956 at a relatively stable
                        rate.</item>
                    <label>5.</label>
                    <item><hi rendition="#italic">Other</hi> (see footnotes ‡ and § to
                        table).</item>
                </list>
